# Data Schema — Spenvo

Document version: **1.0** (M0). Status: baseline draft, versioned with every change.

## 1. Source of truth and model

Two stores, one domain model:

- **Firestore** — remote source of truth (collections below). Writes via native
  offline cache. Deny-by-default rules with server-side roles (draft in
  `firestore.rules`, final in M3).
- **Room + SQLCipher** — encrypted local presentation cache. Provided by `:core:data`.
  Room JSON exports are versioned in `doc/database/schemas/<package>.<DB>/`.

Golden rule: **the UI always reads from Room; writes go to Firestore**.
Conflict: LWW with `editedBy`/`editedAt` (server-set) + visible conflict in the UI.

## 2. Firestore (draft v1.0)

### ER (Mermaid)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USUARIOS ||--o{ ACCESO_PLAN : "accesses"
    PLANES_FINANCIEROS ||--o{ ACCESO_PLAN : "is accessed by"
    PLANES_FINANCIEROS ||--o{ CATEGORIAS : "has"
    PLANES_FINANCIEROS ||--o{ GASTOS : "has"
    PLANES_FINANCIEROS ||--o{ INGRESOS : "has"
    CATEGORIAS ||--o{ GASTOS : "classifies"
    CATEGORIAS ||--o{ INGRESOS : "classifies"
```

### Collections

#### `usuarios/{usuarioId}`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| nombre | string | |
| email | string | (server rules: owner-only read) |
| avatar_url | string? | M7 (Storage) |
| createdAt | timestamp | |
| updatedAt | timestamp | |

#### `planes_financieros/{planId}`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| nombre | string | |
| descripcion | string? | |
| moneda | string | ISO 4217 code |
| createdBy | string | creator uid |
| createdAt | timestamp | |
| updatedAt | timestamp | |
| editedBy | string | server-set (M5) |
| editedAt | timestamp | server-set (M5) |
| deletedAt | timestamp? | soft-delete |

#### `acceso_plan_financiero/{usuarioId}_{planId}` (N:M pivot)
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| usuarioId | string | uid |
| planId | string | |
| rol | enum | `owner` \| `admin` \| `editor` \| `viewer` |
| invitacionEstado | enum | `pendiente` \| `aceptada` (M3) |
| createdAt | timestamp | |
| updatedAt | timestamp | |

#### `categorias/{categoriaId}`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| planId | string | scoped to the plan |
| nombre | string | |
| icono | string | default icon key (M4) |
| iconoUrl | string? | custom icon (M7) |
| tipo | enum | `gasto` \| `ingreso` |
| editedBy | string | |
| editedAt | timestamp | |
| deletedAt | timestamp? | |

#### `gastos/{gastoId}` and `ingresos/{ingresoId}`
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| planId | string | |
| categoriaId | string | |
| monto | number | in minor units of the currency (cents) |
| fecha | date | movement date |
| descripcion | string? | |
| creadoPor | string | uid |
| createdAt | timestamp | |
| updatedAt | timestamp | |
| editedBy | string | server-set (M5) |
| editedAt | timestamp | server-set (M5) |
| deletedAt | timestamp? | soft-delete |

### Cross-cutting conventions
- Amounts always in **minor units** (cents) to avoid floating-point errors.
- `deletedAt != null` = soft-deleted; rules filter it and the UI does not show it.
- `editedBy`/`editedAt` are written by Firestore (rules) with `request.auth.uid` and `request.time`;
  the client never chooses them.

## 3. Room (version 1 — M0)

### `sync_state` (current table)
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | TEXT (PK) | singleton `"default"` |
| lastSyncedAtMillis | INTEGER? | sync metadata (M1/M2) |

### Version plan
- **v1 (M0)**: `sync_state` — validates the Room+KSP+SQLCipher toolchain.
- **v1.1 (M1)**: local domain entities (users, plans, categories, expenses,
  income) as cache; indexes; `editedBy/editedAt`.
- Migrations with `Migration` + SQLCipher (upgrade test included).

## 4. Firestore indexes (draft)

See `firestore.indexes.json`. Rules:
- Index by `planId + fecha` on `gastos` and `ingresos` (monthly listings).
- Index by `planId + tipo` on `categorias`.
- No wildcard indexes.

